From 7d2b02bd77923d7036c7e3c639414a023041c4e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:33:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Observe the submitter-started owner in the Kanban
 restart probe

The real worker reconnects through ensure_gateway_runtime, which starts the
replacement owner itself. The fixture raced it with a second raw gateway.run:
CI rejected that second launcher as already_running, or the fixture accepted
the real owner's ready socket and recorded the losing launcher's PID instead.

Await the real successor's ready control identity and retain its process for
cleanup after the submitter exits. Keep the first launch identity assertion,
all run/session/claim/history checks, and existing readiness/continuation bounds.
Stop submitters before their captured descendants so teardown cannot relaunch.
No production logic or retry policy changes.

Proof:
- Original CI job 132313275430: second launcher rejected by owner PID13215.
- SIGSTOP the probe at the restart gap for12s: old fixture falsely reports
  owner673137 while restart.log identifies actual owner672329; fixed probe
  completes on the actual successor without a competing launch.
- 29/29 original tests with retries disabled, including SIGSTOP/SIGCONT
  150ms stopped /50ms running duty cycle across58 owned processes:238.4s.
- 32/32 tests including three successor readiness/identity controls:68.3s.
- scripts/check --base origin/main:20 checks pass.
